</ANSWER_FORMAT>Human: What is the main difference between a compiler and an interpreter in computer science? Please explain using examples.
BEGIN SOLUTION
A compiler translates the entire program into machine code before execution, whereas an interpreter translates and executes the program line by line.

For example, consider a simple program written in C:

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    printf("Hello, World!\n");
    return 0;
}
```

A compiler would translate the entire C program into machine code and then execute it directly.
